> Actual source diagnostics

These are captured source measurements, in original execution order. They retain weak results and explicit availability flags. Distinct tasks may use different reward scales; a smoke run does not establish convergence.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lunar_lander_diagnostic0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto data=dm::nn::load_npz("build/lunar_lander_source.npz");auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int series=0;for(const auto&[key,t]:data){if(!key.starts_with("outcomes_"))continue;auto y=t.to_vector<double>();if(y.empty())continue;std::vector<double>x(y.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);std::string label=key=="outcomes_0"?"random policy,100 episodes":"heuristic,100 episodes";plot.lines(x,y,label,{37+(series%4)*50,99,235-(series%4)*50});++series;}if(!series)throw std::runtime_error("source diagnostic missing");plot.title("lunar lander actual source diagnostics").x_label("Outcome coordinate: landed / crash / timeout").y_label("Episode count").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/lunar_lander_diagnostic0.svg");}
